  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Melitensin and SNU-387 through multiple pathways, with the core mechanism involving the targeting of CD70 antigen. Melitensin is reported to have a target of CD70, which in turn is targeted by Isohalitulin and SB-269970, both of which also target SNU-387. This indicates that Melitensin may exert its effects through a shared pathway involving CD70, leading to the activation or modulation of SNU-387. The final scores from the paths suggest a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, though the exact mechanism by which Melitensin influences SNU-387 remains to be fully elucidated. The evidence supports a possible role of CD70 in mediating the interaction between Melitensin and SNU-387, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct interaction and functional significance.",
